{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q219037","formula":"C₆H₁₈LiNSi₂","hill":"C6H18LiNSi2","elements":["H","Li","C","N","Si"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":18.0,"N":1.0,"Li":1.0,"Si":2.0},"names":{"en":"Lithium bis(trimethylsilyl)amide","ru":"Бис(триметилсилил)амид лития"},"descriptions":{"en":"Lithium bis(trimethylsilyl)amide is a lithiated organosilicon compound with the formula LiN(Si(CH3)3)2. It is commonly abbreviated as LiHMDS or Li(HMDS) (lithium hexamethyldisilazide - a reference to its conjugate acid HMDS) and is primarily used as a strong non-nucleophilic base and as a ligand. Like many lithium reagents, it has a tendency to aggregate and will form a cyclic trimer in the absence of coordinating species.","ru":"Бис(триметилсилил)амид лития (Lithium hexamethyldisilazide — LiHMDS) — химическое соединение с формулой LiN[(CH3)3Si]2. Образует бесцветные кристаллы, разлагается на воздухе с самовоспламенением, стабилен в инертной атмосфере. Растворяется в инертных органических растворителях."},"fame":19,"pubchemCid":2733832,"mass":167.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"[Li+].C[Si](C)(C)[N-][Si](C)(C)C","inchikey":"YNESATAKKCNGOF-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"lithium bis(trimethylsilyl)azanide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"2733832","atoms":28,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.966,"y":0.846,"z":1.115,"el":"C"},{"x":1.465,"y":-0.361,"z":-0.221,"el":"Si"},{"x":2.793,"y":-0.294,"z":-1.569,"el":"C"},{"x":1.466,"y":-2.106,"z":0.467,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.059,"y":0.021,"z":-0.99,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.467,"y":0.372,"z":-0.013,"el":"Si"},{"x":-1.374,"y":2.091,"z":0.731,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.962,"y":0.35,"z":-1.174,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.79,"y":-0.884,"z":1.334,"el":"C"},{"x":1.913,"y":1.878,"z":0.754,"el":"H"},{"x":1.326,"y":0.754,"z":1.997,"el":"H"},{"x":2.995,"y":0.656,"z":1.4